steps.rationale:
internal/rae generates class-conditional ImageNet images, matched to the PyTorch reference: the ViT-XL decoder, the DiT-DH velocity, and Euler over the reference's shifted grid. Only tests call it. Serve it through the image-gen capability, as the other image models are:
- a module in the recipe catalog;
- a resolver for the collection directory: the DiT checkpoint, decoder, latent statistics and the DINOv2 encoder's image processor;
- a request naming an ImageNet class and a seed;
- classifier-free guidance when the reference's sampler config uses it.
cmd/validate then gives RAE its image proof, and user-scorecard's validate-all-models loses its last unvalidated model.

Registering the module edits internal/modelrecipe, an inference-surface root, which would expire every text model's guard. So this row waits on surface-without-capability-tables. Predicted effect: first-output and held-out-quality become measurable for RAE on the image route.

Serves: RAE image generation for users. Evidence: the activation run is both the acceptance and the RAE scorecard row. Batch: surface.
